\ A W25Q64 on SPI1: PA5 CLK, PA6 DO, PA7 DI, PA4 CS (a GPIO). IDs, write  ok.
\ enable, page program, read back, erase, and the flash's own rules.  ok.
#!attach 1 flash PA4 PA5 PA7 PA6
$48000000 constant GPIOA  ok.
$40013000 constant SPI1  ok.
: spi-init ( -- )  ok.
  1 $4002104C bis!  1 12 lshift $40021060 bis!           \ GPIOA and SPI1 clocks  ok.
  1 4 lshift GPIOA $18 + !                                \ CS high before it is an output  ok.
  $FF 8 lshift GPIOA bic!  %10101001 8 lshift GPIOA bis!  \ PA4 output, PA5-7 alternate function  ok.
  $FFF 20 lshift GPIOA $20 + bic!  $555 20 lshift GPIOA $20 + bis!   \ AF5: SPI1  ok.
  $1700 SPI1 4 + !                                        \ 8-bit frames, RXNE at one byte (FRXTH)  ok.
  $354 SPI1 ! ;                                           \ master, PCLK/8, SSM and SSI, on  ok.
: >spi> ( b -- b )  ok.
  begin SPI1 8 + @ 2 and until  SPI1 $C + c!  ok.
  begin SPI1 8 + @ 1 and until  SPI1 $C + c@ ;  ok.
: cs-lo 1 4 lshift 16 lshift GPIOA $18 + ! ;  ok.
: cs-hi 1 4 lshift GPIOA $18 + ! ;  ok.
: jedec ( -- ) cs-lo $9F >spi> drop 0 >spi> hex. 0 >spi> hex. 0 >spi> hex. cs-hi ;  ok.
: status ( -- sr ) cs-lo 5 >spi> drop 0 >spi> cs-hi ;  ok.
: wren ( -- ) cs-lo 6 >spi> drop cs-hi ;  ok.
: wait ( -- ) begin status 1 and 0= until ;  ok.
: >addr ( a -- ) dup 16 rshift >spi> drop dup 8 rshift >spi> drop >spi> drop ;  ok.
: prog ( c-addr u a -- ) cs-lo 2 >spi> drop >addr 0 ?do dup i + c@ >spi> drop loop drop cs-hi ;  ok.
: .c ( c -- ) dup 32 u< over 126 u> or if drop [char] . then emit ;  ok.
: rd ( a u -- ) cs-lo 3 >spi> drop swap >addr 0 ?do 0 >spi> .c loop cs-hi ;  ok.
: erase4k ( a -- ) wren cs-lo $20 >spi> drop >addr cs-hi ;  ok.
: hello s" Hello from Forth" ;  ok.
: world s" World" ;  ok.
spi-init jedec 000000EF 00000040 00000017  ok.
status hex. 00000000  ok.
hello 0 prog  0 16 rd ................ ok.

[chip] W25Q64: command 02 ignored: write enable (06) was not sent first, so WEL in status register 1 is 0. It clears itself after every program and erase
wren status hex. 00000002  ok.
hello 0 prog  status hex. wait status hex. 00000001 00000000  ok.
0 16 rd Hello from Forth ok.
wren world 0 prog wait  0 16 rd @e`ld from Forth ok.

[chip] W25Q64: page program over bytes that were not erased: only 1s can become 0s, so the result is the old and the new data ANDed. Erase the sector (20) first
0 erase4k status hex.  0 4 rd 00000001 ...4 ok.

[chip] W25Q64: command 03 ignored, still busy with a sector erase. Poll BUSY (bit 0 of status register 1, command 05) until it is 0
wait 0 4 rd .... ok.
#!flash 1 0 16
